---
// Migrated verbatim from public/topics/system-design-practice/lessons/0003-starter-url-shortener.html (URL unchanged: builds to 0003-starter-url-shortener.html).
// Body is is:raw: braces/inline scripts/JSON blocks pass through untouched.
import Lesson from "../../../../layouts/Lesson.astro";
const titlePt = "Brief L1 — Encurtador de URL";
const titleEn = "Brief L1 — URL shortener";
const titleFallback = "URL shortener brief";
const bodyClass = "lang-pt";
const viewport = "width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0";
const assets = [
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/style.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/dark.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/i18n.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/exercises.css\" />",
	"<script src=\"../assets/i18n.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/nav.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/exercises.js\" defer></script>",
];

---
<Lesson
	titlePt={titlePt}
	titleEn={titleEn}
	titleFallback={titleFallback}
	bodyClass={bodyClass}
	viewport={viewport}
	assets={assets}
>
	<Fragment is:raw>
    <article class="lesson">
      <header class="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow"
          >⬡ Dojo · <span data-lang="pt">Brief L1 · 25 min</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Brief L1 · 25 min</span></span
        >
        <h1>
          <span data-lang="pt">Encurtador de URL.</span
          ><span data-lang="en">URL shortener.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lead">
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >O problema canônico para aprender o loop inteiro (clarificar →
            estimar → desenhar → um tradeoff) sem concorrência.
            <strong
              >Alvo: desenhar 4 caixas em 5 min e narrar um caminho de leitura e
              um de escrita.</strong
            ></span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >The canonical problem to learn the whole loop (clarify → estimate →
            draw → one tradeoff) without concurrency.
            <strong
              >Goal: draw 4 boxes in 5 min and narrate one read path and one
              write path.</strong
            ></span
          >
        </p>
        <p class="lesson-nav-top">
          ↑
          <a href="0002-the-difficulty-ladder.html"
            ><span data-lang="pt">Escada</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Ladder</span></a
          >
          · <span data-lang="pt">próximo:</span
          ><span data-lang="en">next:</span>
          <a href="0004-starter-onboarding-email.html"
            ><span data-lang="pt">Onboarding+email</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Onboarding+email</span></a
          >
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="callout key">
        <p>
          <strong
            ><span data-lang="pt">O prompt (fale em voz alta):</span
            ><span data-lang="en">The prompt (say it aloud):</span></strong
          >
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >“Desenhe um encurtador de URL como o bit.ly. O usuário cola uma URL
            longa, recebe um código curto; quem acessa o código curto é
            redirecionado.”</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >“Design a URL shortener like bit.ly. A user pastes a long URL, gets
            a short code; anyone hitting the short code is redirected.”</span
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">1</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Clarifique primeiro (2 min)</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Clarify first (2 min)</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="kicker">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Não comece a desenhar. Pergunte. Cada resposta muda o desenho.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Don't start drawing. Ask. Each answer changes the design.</span
        >
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            ><strong>Read/write:</strong> quantos redirecionamentos vs quantas
            criações? (geralmente 100:1 — leitura pesada).</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            ><strong>Read/write:</strong> how many redirects vs how many
            creates? (usually 100:1 — read-heavy).</span
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            ><strong>Apelido custom?</strong> o usuário escolhe o código, ou
            geramos?</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            ><strong>Custom alias?</strong> the user picks the code, or we
            generate it?</span
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            ><strong>Expira?</strong> os links vivem para sempre?</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            ><strong>Expiry?</strong> do links live forever?</span
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            ><strong>Analytics?</strong> contamos cliques? (muda o desenho —
            vira um write adicional.)</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            ><strong>Analytics?</strong> do we count clicks? (changes the design
            — becomes an extra write.)</span
          >
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">2</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Estimativa (2 min, sem congelar)</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Estimate (2 min, don't freeze)</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>
                <span data-lang="pt">Quantidade</span
                ><span data-lang="en">Quantity</span>
              </th>
              <th>
                <span data-lang="pt">Estimativa</span
                ><span data-lang="en">Estimate</span>
              </th>
              <th>
                <span data-lang="pt">Por quê</span
                ><span data-lang="en">Why</span>
              </th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>
                <span data-lang="pt">URLs criadas</span
                ><span data-lang="en">URLs created</span>
              </td>
              <td>~100M</td>
              <td>
                <span data-lang="pt">chute razoável</span
                ><span data-lang="en">reasonable guess</span>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                <span data-lang="pt">Redirecionamentos</span
                ><span data-lang="en">Redirects</span>
              </td>
              <td>~10B</td>
              <td>
                <span data-lang="pt">100× criações</span
                ><span data-lang="en">100× creates</span>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                <span data-lang="pt">Tamanho do código</span
                ><span data-lang="en">Code size</span>
              </td>
              <td>7 chars</td>
              <td>
                <span data-lang="pt"
                  >base62 (a-z A-Z 0-9) → 62⁷ ≈ 3,5 trilhões. Suficiente.</span
                ><span data-lang="en"
                  >base62 (a-z A-Z 0-9) → 62⁷ ≈ 3.5 trillion. Enough.</span
                >
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                <span data-lang="pt">Armazenamento</span
                ><span data-lang="en">Storage</span>
              </td>
              <td>~10 GB</td>
              <td>
                <span data-lang="pt">100M × ~100 bytes cada</span
                ><span data-lang="en">100M × ~100 bytes each</span>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="callout tip">
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            ><strong>O número que importa:</strong> leitura &gt;&gt; escrita.
            Isso justifica um <strong>cache</strong> na frente do banco para
            redirecionamentos quentes. Pronto — você já tem a justificativa de
            um componente.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            ><strong>The number that matters:</strong> read &gt;&gt; write. That
            justifies a <strong>cache</strong> in front of the DB for hot
            redirects. Done — you've justified a component.</span
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">3</span><span data-lang="pt">Desenhe (5 min)</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Draw (5 min)</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="scroll-x" style="margin: 18px 0">
        <svg
          viewBox="0 0 720 240"
          width="100%"
          style="min-width: 660px"
          role="img"
          aria-labelledby="url-t"
        >
          <title
            id="url-t"
            data-pt="Cliente → API → Cache → DB; serviço de código gera o alias"
            data-en="Client → API → Cache → DB; a code service generates the alias"
          >
            URL shortener
          </title>
          <defs>
            <marker
              id="ua"
              markerWidth="8"
              markerHeight="8"
              refX="6"
              refY="3"
              orient="auto"
            >
              <path d="M0,0 L0,6 L7,3 z" fill="#8b6ff7" />
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <g font-family="Space Grotesk" font-size="12" font-weight="700">
            <rect
              x="20"
              y="90"
              width="90"
              height="50"
              rx="10"
              fill="#211d33"
              stroke="#2dd4bf"
            />
            <text x="65" y="119" fill="#2dd4bf" text-anchor="middle">
              Cliente
            </text>
            <rect
              x="180"
              y="90"
              width="90"
              height="50"
              rx="10"
              fill="#211d33"
              stroke="#8b6ff7"
            />
            <text x="225" y="119" fill="#8b6ff7" text-anchor="middle">API</text>
            <rect
              x="330"
              y="50"
              width="100"
              height="44"
              rx="10"
              fill="#0c2a27"
              stroke="#2dd4bf"
            />
            <text x="380" y="77" fill="#2dd4bf" text-anchor="middle">
              Cache
            </text>
            <rect
              x="330"
              y="130"
              width="100"
              height="50"
              rx="10"
              fill="#2a1207"
              stroke="#f59e0b"
            />
            <text x="380" y="153" fill="#fbbf24" text-anchor="middle">DB</text>
            <rect
              x="180"
              y="185"
              width="120"
              height="40"
              rx="9"
              fill="#0c2a27"
              stroke="#2dd4bf"
            />
            <text x="240" y="209" fill="#2dd4bf" text-anchor="middle">
              gerador de código
            </text>
          </g>
          <g
            stroke="#8b6ff7"
            stroke-width="2"
            fill="none"
            marker-end="url(#ua)"
          >
            <path d="M110 115 H180" />
            <path d="M270 105 H330" />
            <path d="M380 94 H330" opacity="0" />
            <path d="M270 140 C300 140 300 150 330 155" />
          </g>
          <g
            stroke="#2dd4bf"
            stroke-width="2"
            fill="none"
            stroke-dasharray="4 4"
            marker-end="url(#ua)"
          >
            <path d="M240 185 V140" />
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          ><strong>Narração (diga isso):</strong> “O cliente chama a API. Para
          <em>criar</em>, a API pede um código ao gerador e grava no DB (codigo
          → url longa). Para <em>redirecionar</em>, a API procura no cache; se
          não achar, busca no DB e devolve um redirect HTTP.”</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          ><strong>Narration (say this):</strong> “The client calls the API. To
          <em>create</em>, the API asks the code generator for a code and stores
          it in the DB (code → long url). To <em>redirect</em>, the API checks
          the cache; on a miss it reads the DB and returns an HTTP
          redirect.”</span
        >
      </p>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">4</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">O tradeoff para falar (1 min)</span
        ><span data-lang="en">The tradeoff to state (1 min)</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="ex classify" id="ex-code">
        <div class="ex-head">
          <h3>
            <span data-lang="pt">Como gerar o código curto?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">How to generate the short code?</span>
          </h3>
        </div>
        <div
          class="ex-item"
          data-correct="random"
          data-explain-pt="Aleatório é simples e sem coordenação: gere 7 chars, cheque colisão (rara com 3,5T de espaço), grave. Tradeoff: precisa checar colisão, mas é raro."
          data-explain-en="Random is simple and needs no coordination: generate 7 chars, check for collision (rare with 3.5T space), store. Tradeoff: must check for collision, but it's rare."
        >
          <div class="ex-stem">
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Gere 7 chars aleatórios, cheque colisão, grave.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >Generate 7 random chars, check collision, store.</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="ex-opts">
            <button class="ex-opt" data-pick="random">
              <span data-lang="pt">Aleatório + checa colisão</span
              ><span data-lang="en">Random + check collision</span></button
            ><button class="ex-opt" data-pick="counter">
              <span data-lang="pt">Contador global incrementado</span
              ><span data-lang="en">Global incrementing counter</span>
            </button>
          </div>
          <div class="ex-fb"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <details>
        <summary>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >A resposta completa (abrir só depois de tentar)</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >The full answer (open only after attempting)</span
          >
        </summary>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              ><strong>Gerar código:</strong> aleatório base62. Colisão é rara
              (3,5T espaço); um <code>SELECT … WHERE code=</code> resolve.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              ><strong>Generate code:</strong> random base62. Collision is rare
              (3.5T space); a <code>SELECT … WHERE code=</code> handles
              it.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              ><strong>Cache:</strong> Redis para os códigos quentes; TTL
              opcional. Resolve 100:1.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              ><strong>Cache:</strong> Redis for hot codes; optional TTL. Solves
              the 100:1 ratio.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              ><strong>Falhas neste nível:</strong> colisão (regra), cache miss
              (DB aguenta), analytics via fila assíncrona (não no caminho do
              redirect).</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              ><strong>Failures at this level:</strong> collision (rule), cache
              miss (DB handles it), analytics via an async queue (off the
              redirect path).</span
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              ><strong>Não precisa:</strong> shardar, consensus, locks. É
              L1.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              ><strong>You don't need:</strong> sharding, consensus, locks. It's
              L1.</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </details>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">5</span><span data-lang="pt">Auto-avaliação</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Self-review</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="callout info">
        <p>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Grave 25 min. Depois marque: (1) perguntei 2+ coisas antes de
            desenhar? (2) estimei 1 número e justifiquei um componente com ele?
            (3) desenhei 4 caixas narrando leitura E escrita? (4) falei 1
            tradeoff? Se sim em 3+, passe para o próximo brief.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >Record 25 min. Then check: (1) did I ask 2+ things before drawing?
            (2) did I estimate 1 number and use it to justify a component? (3)
            did I draw 4 boxes narrating BOTH read AND write? (4) did I state 1
            tradeoff? If yes on 3+, move to the next brief.</span
          >
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="cite">
        <span data-lang="pt">Próximo nível →</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Next level →</span>
        <a href="0004-starter-onboarding-email.html"
          ><span data-lang="pt">Onboarding + email (ClearOne)</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Onboarding + email (ClearOne)</span></a
        >
      </p>
    </article>
  </Fragment>
</Lesson>
